1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
If you want to perform a full production deployment, then you need to make a few configuration decisions.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This video explains the choices that you need to make and how they impact the installation process.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Before planning your setup, take some time to familiarise yourself with the system's architecture and system requirements,

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
as these may affect the decisions that you make.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
You can find these resources in our online documentation.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Burp Suite Enterprise Edition includes an embedded H2 database.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Using this database makes it easy for you to evaluate the product or run trials,

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
but for production deployments, you may want to connect to an external database.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
If you are using an external database, you must set it up before installing Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
For more information on this process, see our setting up the external database document.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
It's worth noting that you can migrate from the embedded database to an external database later, if required,

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
For standard deployments, you'll need to choose a port that users and API clients can use to access the application.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The port number you choose must meet the following requirements.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The port must be available for use on the machine that you want to install the enterprise and web servers on.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
And the operating system must be allowed to bind to that port.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
On Linux and macOS, low privilege users are unable to bind to some well-known port numbers.

